# Cloudflare routing.
#
# Two single-page apps share one origin and one deploy:
#
#   /docs/*   the documentation site, built with base=/docs/
#   /*        the landing page + demo workspace
#
# `not_found_handling: single-page-application` in wrangler.jsonc sends any
# unknown path to the root index.html, which is right for the app but wrong for
# the docs: a direct hit on /docs/pipeline would load the app shell. These rules
# run first and pin the /docs subtree to the docs shell. Order matters — the
# first match wins, so the narrow /docs rules sit above the catch-all.

# Docs: the bare path and any client route resolve to the docs shell.
/docs        /docs/index.html   200
/docs/*      /docs/index.html   200

# App: any other unknown path resolves to the app shell. Real files (assets,
# favicons, /docs/*) are served before this rule is ever reached.
/*           /index.html        200
